In my experience, asking for help, discussing the game, reading
spoilers, and "source diving" are *not* considered cheating by the
community.  It is, however, considered by many to be "more fun" to
figure it out for yourself, and someone who ascended without external
help would certainly impress many people.

Part of the reason for this is that the game is distributed as source;
as you've been given the source, reading it as your way of learning
about the game is widely considered to be a reasonable action.

Preserving save files is different; this is working around a
designed-in source of difficulty in the game.  A player who does so is
thus not really playing the same game at all.  Just as "explore mode"
ascensions aren't considered to be "the real thing" by the community,
so for those achieved via save file preservation.


